# Recipe: secure app communication

Use the P2P library's encrypted transport and explicit pairing/grants. Define
validated app methods and event streams with `/rpc`; host/connect via `/service`
or the existing root node. Read `modules/p2p.mdc` and `add-encrypted-channels`.

Do not wrap library connections in another SecretStream, replace their Protomux,
or open a parallel swarm. Discovery is not authorization. Issue scoped invites,
reject ungranted methods, honor cancellation and bound output. Persist app-owned
history locally for offline use. Encryption in transit does not provide at-rest
encryption or erase data already received. Validate permission denial and
stream shutdown on disconnect before claiming secure app behavior.
